{
    "//": [
        "The layering contract, machine-readable because it is no longer enforced",
        "for free.",
        "",
        "Today the package manager is the enforcement: runtime-sof cannot import",
        "runtime-trinity because it is not a dependency, and no manifest edit passes",
        "review unnoticed. Inside one package that guarantee disappears at exactly",
        "the moment the barrier becomes a one-line import. This file replaces it.",
        "",
        "`mayImport` is exhaustive: a directory may import from itself and from the",
        "layers listed, and from nothing else. Layer names are directory paths, so",
        "the ordering INSIDE global is enforced too -- math is not allowed to reach",
        "sideways into model just because both are global."
    ],
    "surfaces": {
        "index.js": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity",
                "sof",
                "audio",
                "character",
                "input",
                "core"
            ]
        },
        "global/index.js": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model"
            ]
        }
    },
    "externalImports": [
        "gl-matrix",
        "meshoptimizer",
        "yaml"
    ],
    "externalDynamicImports": [
        "resource/worker/CjsResManWorker.js"
    ],
    "layers": {
        "global/utils": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/math"
            ]
        },
        "global/math": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/consts"
            ]
        },
        "global/consts": {
            "mayImport": []
        },
        "global/schema": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts"
            ]
        },
        "global/model": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/schema"
            ]
        },
        "global/contracts": {
            "mayImport": []
        },
        "resource": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model"
            ]
        },
        "trinity": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource"
            ]
        },
        "sof": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource"
            ],
            "why": [
                "SOF is standalone and trinity is NOT in its list, which is the whole",
                "point of writing this down. SOF emits a graph that names Trinity and",
                "audio classes; naming a class is not importing it, and a consumer",
                "supplies the constructors. The day someone 'just imports Trinity here'",
                "the build fails instead of the property quietly disappearing."
            ]
        },
        "audio": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource"
            ]
        },
        "character": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity"
            ]
        },
        "input": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model"
            ]
        },
        "engine/webgpu": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity"
            ],
            "why": [
                "The implemented backend extends canonical dependency-floor, resource,",
                "and Trinity contracts. It never imports core, tools, or another engine."
            ]
        },
        "core": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity",
                "sof",
                "audio",
                "character",
                "input",
                "engine/webgpu"
            ],
            "why": [
                "Composition. It is allowed to know about everything below it, which is",
                "exactly why nothing below is allowed to know about it."
            ]
        },
        "tools": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity",
                "sof",
                "audio",
                "character",
                "input",
                "engine/webgpu",
                "core"
            ],
            "why": [
                "The top layer, and off the default export surface. It may reach down to",
                "everything; nothing may reach up to it. Browser-safe tooling only --",
                "acquisition, emulation, realtime. The Node-only suite stays a separate",
                "package, so this name must never become a home for native dependencies.",
                "",
                "A runtime module wanting something from here means the value belongs",
                "lower down instead; tools/perobject is the live candidate."
            ]
        }
    }
}
